  "substantive_analysis_of_the_core_debate": {
    "camp_72_arguments": [
      "1. Internal Pareto improvement / Coalitional rationality: Coalition N (size 8, budget 16) can autonomously provide (9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9). In the (9,8,8,8,8,8,8,8) committee, Voter 1 is indifferent between keeping their 2nd private candidate vs. taking candidate 8, so Voter 1 shouldn't veto a Pareto improvement for the other 7 members.",
      "2. Strong Pareto optimality: The c = 7 committee is weakly Pareto dominated by swapping 1 private candidate for common candidate 8, which camp 72 argues disqualifies it from the Core."
    ],
    "camp_65_definitive_refutation": [
      "1. Explicit Literature Definition: In ABC voting (Aziz et al. 2017, Section 4; Peters 2018; Lackner & Skowron 2023, Def 4.1), 'the Core' is universally defined with STRICT improvement for EVERY member of S: \\forall i \\in S, |A(i) \\cap T| > |A(i) \\cap W|.",
